[agent]
name = "bake-off"
version = "0.2.0"
description = "HarnessQL flash bake-off lane: iterate a GraphQL schema per the Composition Guide, reason-backed cost/benefit. Portable: no scratch path, no key file."
entry_stage = "bake"

[read_paths]
# GQL-09 removed the scratch-path dependence. This lane needs NOTHING outside its
# run workdir: the caller stages the seeds there, the schema generations ship in
# study/, and the Composition Guide is a bundled tool. So there is no absolute
# box path and no `~/` catch-all left to re-point on a fresh install:
#   - the guide: tools/composition_guide.rhai (read it with the tool, not a path),
#     generated from references/composition-guide.md by scripts/generate_tools.py.
#   - seeds and output: inside the workdir the caller passes with --workdir.
# An old checkout that still wants the scratch study directory can stage it into
# the workdir, or set HARNESSQL_LEGACY_STUDY for the Python drivers, which is an
# explicit opt-in rather than a default.
allow = []

[tool_permissions]
read_file     = "allow"
list_dir      = "allow"
context_read  = "allow"
context_write = "allow"
context_list  = "allow"
write_file    = "allow"
submit_output = "allow"

[context.regions]
task         = { kind = "pinned", budget = "10%", max_tokens = 6000, required = true, seed = { caller = "task" } }
conversation = { kind = "sliding_window", budget = "50%", max_tokens = 16000, max_items = 14 }

[stages.bake]
mode = "autonomous"
model = { models = [ { provider = "openrouter", model = "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash" } ] , allow_user_default = false, request_timeout_secs = 1800 }
available_tools = ["composition_guide", "read_file", "list_dir", "context_write", "write_file", "submit_output"]
require_output = true
allow_complete = true
required_tools = ["submit_output"]
max_iterations = 60
system_prompt = """You are a HarnessQL bake-off lane. You ITERATE on an existing GraphQL schema to make it better per the Composition Guide — you do NOT start from scratch.

Your file tools are confined to the workdir this run was started in. Everything you need is either a tool or a path inside that workdir; there is no scratch directory to look for.

CRITICAL: Your stage REQUIRES you to call the submit_output tool. You CANNOT complete without it. After you write_file your final schema, you MUST call submit_output (a one-line 'BAKE <label> complete'). Do not spend iterations refining forever — produce your best iterated schema, write it, and submit. If you reach ~50 iterations and are not done, STOP refining and submit what you have (a complete-but-imperfect output is far better than a run that never submits).

STEP 1: call the `composition_guide` tool (no arguments). It returns the Composition Guide, your arbiter for every change. It is a bundled static reference, so it works from any install directory; do NOT go looking for composition-guide.md on disk.

STEP 2: The TASK string carries:
   - seeds=<semicolon-separated paths to the schema candidate(s) you are iterating on>
   - out=<path of the file you must write your revised schema to>
   - level=<N> lane=<0/1> label=<this lane's label>
Parse these. Read the paths from seeds= exactly as given (they are staged inside your workdir). read_file EVERY seed path; if there are 2, they are two perspectives of the same abstraction — you must reconcile/merge them into a coherent best-of-both, NOT concatenate.

STEP 3: Produce an ITERATED schema. Rules:
- Every change vs the seed(s) must be deliberate and guided by the Composition Guide.
- After the schema, produce a 'RATIONALE' section listing EVERY change as:
      CHANGE <descriptor>
        DRIVER: <which guide rule/section>
        COST: <what it adds/removes in types/fields/complexity>
        BENEFIT: <what it improves — clarity, type-safety, renderability, less drift>
- Do NOT invent unrelated rework. Iterate the abstraction you were given.
- Do NOT write comments ('#') anywhere. Emit clean SDL only — comments are noise and are stripped downstream. Put the RATIONALE section in your submit_output text, not in the schema file.
- Output FULL Monty, un-capped.
- Once you have written the schema: write_file to EXACTLY <out>. NEVER use your label as the filename. THEN IMMEDIATELY submit_output the RATIONALE section. These two calls finish your work — do them back-to-back."""
